fix(ui): F-0031 regression — sensor status words fit at 320 px

Regression named by the round-1 fix review (run 20261006-160411-fix-review): at 320 px the new
OK/Check/Fault words sat behind the table edge ("Che", "Faul"). The Sensors table was already wider than its
card at 320 px before any fix; the clipped "Status" header in the baseline shows this.
Baseline: apply after F-0032.patch (round 2).

Contract
  Originating: at 320 px (both states) every status word and the Status header are fully visible without
  horizontal scrolling.
  Regression: full audit; journey switch-dosing-to-manual; no introduced finding; no ARIA loss; pixel change
  limited to widths of 384 px or less.
  Scope: styles.css, a narrow-screen rule scoped to #sensors.
Drift class and layer: local defect; CSS only. Below 24rem the Sensors cells use 4 px horizontal padding instead
of 7 px, and the dot-to-word gap is 4 px instead of 8 px. Nothing changes at wider widths.
Re-test: run 20261006-160813-fix-r1-320 (full audit, compared with the round-1 run).
  Findings: 0 introduced and 0 introduced instances. ARIA: 12 snapshots, 0 changed. Visual: only the 320 and 375 px captures
  changed (rows got shorter because the names fit on one line). The journey passed (3/3).

